D7.body:
A few days on, I came across this again — your words:

{echo}

Nobody's waiting on anything from you. Come back whenever you feel like it.

D14.body:
It took something out of you to write this:

{echo}

I remember. That's all I wanted to say.

D21.body:
Some things get lighter the moment they're said out loud. You said:

{echo}

That lightness was real.

D30.body:
A month ago, you said:

{echo}

A person and their own words can drift apart. Reading it now — does it land the same way?

D66.body:
Every step of the road you walked is still on the map. This is still on it:

{echo}

Whenever you want to look at it again, it's there.

D90.body:
Three months ago, you wrote a letter. It's still here.

{echo}

The person who wrote it has probably come a little further since.
